            <description sparkle:format="plain-text"><![CDATA[Commit: 761a9103099994d95598b3d753b1232c035b385b
Channel: beta

fix(scene): apply container visibility gates to the render graph

Container layers hid themselves through SceneNode::SetVisible alone, but
graph build only reads the elision set, so a user property gating a whole
group (weekday component, language variant) never reached the renderer.
The load-time binding pass then re-lit each child on its own font-variant
binding, leaving both language groups drawn until the user toggled the
property once. Mark user-gated containers elidable, and let SetNodeVisible
queue same-value calls whenever the elision set disagrees with the node
flag so a parse-time hide can still be picked up.

Also route text layers through EnsureScriptScene so engine.userProperties
and the bone resolvers are seeded when a text layer is the first object to
need a JS runtime, resolve effect visibility bindings for text objects,
and write a visible-bound script's return value back to layer visibility.

]]></description>
